    "question": {
      ":question/id": "96f6b885-0020-5991-a2fd-41ea50940dc6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "If $\\cos x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ then $\\cos (x-2\\pi )=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-1$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x=\\cos (x+2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ then $\\cos (x-2\\pi )=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
